From 38f3a0dcc0c51e75060bda7c07d67f54b6b5ba8c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 15:06:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Four windows the 377 cache draws, and the locs that have been
 offering them all along

Right-click a furnace and it says "Smelt". Right-click a dairy churn and it says
"Churn". Right-click Ellis and he says "Trade". Seven furnace locs, two churns and
one tanner in the cache carry those ops, no trigger in this content answered any of
them, and clicking produced no error and no log line. Same shape as Lvl-6 Enchant and
the four unwired spellbook buttons: the cache is ahead of the content, and the symptom
of the gap is silence.

The panels those ops should open were in scripts/interfaces/ the whole time, named
inter_53, inter_306, inter_282 and inter_315/316/317, with every component called
com_<n>. claude/cache-interface-survey.md found them by printing what they say.

ADOPTING A CACHE PANEL IS NOW A TOOL. tools/genadopt.py renames an interface and its
components, moves the file where the skill lives, and re-takes every id in
interface.pack and interface.order. It derives the names from the panel's OWN TEXT -
"Smelt 1 @lre@Silver" becomes smelt_1_silver - rather than a list somebody typed, and
that matters for one concrete reason: the panel's columns run Bronze, Iron, SILVER,
STEEL while smelting.struct lists them Bronze, Iron, STEEL, SILVER. A hand-written map
would have swapped two columns and nothing would have noticed. Six panels went through
it, and each one renders pixel-identical to the cache file it replaced.

NO NEW NUMBERS FOR THREE OF THE FOUR. Smelting reads the smelting_struct each bar obj
already carries. Tanning reads the ^tanner_*_cost constants tanner.constant already
holds - both sets, because Canifis is 2/5/45 against Al Kharid's 1/3/20 and that is not
a fixed markup. Silver casting reads crafting_jewelry_struct, the same struct the old
seven-branch p_choice cascade read. ~smelt_bar is lifted out of [label,smelt_ore] so
the window and the use-an-ore-on-the-furnace path are one implementation, not two.

THE CHURN IS THE ONE THAT HAD NOTHING BEHIND IT. Three panels, three inputs: milk makes
all three products, cream makes butter and cheese, butter makes cheese. Every level and
every experience figure is off that product's own OSRS wiki page, and the pages agree
with each other in a way worth checking - all four routes from milk to cheese pay
exactly 640.

JAGEX'S OWN CONFIG NAMED THE SILVER PRODUCTS. scripts/_unpack/727/all.inv carries seven
single-slot inventories, one per slot of this panel, each stocking the product that slot
shows, all seven already packed and none ever used. They identify the three the panel's
English does not: the lightning rod is fenk_conductor, the demonic sigil is agrith_sigil,
the silvthrill rod is burgh_rod_command1. An earlier draft of this round said those three
had no obj in the build - a negative from a hand-guessed name, and wrong. Four of the
seven are wired; the other three are quest steps with no Crafting level or experience
anywhere to copy, and nothing hands out their moulds, so their slots stay on the
you-need-the-mould side without a line of code making that happen.

tools/silentops.py is the companion to interfaceindex.py: which op labels the cache
advertises that no loc in the game answers. 114 before this round, 112 after.

windows_battery.py is 9 groups, ALL PASS, anchored on the loc and npc configs, the 727
inventories, smelting.struct and tanner.constant - none of which this round wrote.
windows_mutate.py breaks 20 things and every one is caught by its own check.

